<title>VENEZUELA: Venezuela's Manpa absorbs affiliates.</title>
<headline>Venezuela's Manpa absorbs affiliates.</headline>
<dateline>CARACAS 1997-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Venezuela paper and pulp manufacturer Manpa said Monday it had absorbed its two main subsidiaries to reduce administrative costs.</p>
<p>Sanitary paper manufacturer CA Fabrica de Papel de Maracay and office and school stationary producer Corporacion Industrial Alpes SA would be fused into the holding company Manufacturas de Papel CA, Manpa said in a release.</p>
<p>&quot;The fusion consolidates a series of processes which have been duplicated such as accounting, information etc which will generate savings of about 2.5 billion bolivars ($5.1 million),&quot; Manpa said.</p>
<p>((-- Caracas newsroom, 582 505 2600))</p>
